{"question_id": "NHQ-CCNA-8D70F783-90A5-4322-A35B-4F0D631055B0", "chapter_id": "CCNA-D1", "topic_id": "CCNA-D1-T05", "concept_tag": "core", "difficulty": "medium", "format": "mcq", "competency": "application", "stem": "How many usable host addresses are available in a /26 subnet?", "options": ["30", "62", "64", "126"], "correct": ["B"], "explanation": "A /26 subnet has 6 host bits: 2^6 = 64 total addresses minus 2 (network + broadcast) = 62 usable hosts.", "marks": 1, "source": {"kind": "nhprep_quiz", "ref": "nhprep:quiz/ccna/8d70f783-90a5-4322-a35b-4f0d631055b0"}, "lesson_ref": null, "key_origin": "nhprep"}
