{"question_id": "NHQ-CCNA-CFD14663-FDAD-4966-BE6E-9434173E3B3E", "chapter_id": "CCNA-D1", "topic_id": "CCNA-D1-T08", "concept_tag": "core", "difficulty": "easy", "format": "mcq", "competency": "knowledge_understanding", "stem": "Which IPv6 address type is equivalent to a private IPv4 address?", "options": ["Global unicast", "Unique local (FC00::/7)", "Link-local (FE80::/10)", "Multicast (FF00::/8)"], "correct": ["B"], "explanation": "Unique local addresses (FC00::/7) are the IPv6 equivalent of RFC 1918 private addresses — routable internally but not on the public internet.", "marks": 1, "source": {"kind": "nhprep_quiz", "ref": "nhprep:quiz/ccna/cfd14663-fdad-4966-be6e-9434173e3b3e"}, "lesson_ref": null, "key_origin": "nhprep"}
